  "problemStatement": {
    "formal": "**Theorem (crtPi)**: For a pairwise-coprime family ns : Fin k → ℕ (i ≠ j ⟹ Coprime (ns i) (ns j)),\n  ZMod (∏ i, ns i) ≃+* ∀ i : Fin k, ZMod (ns i)\nas rings, indexed symmetrically by Fin k.",
    "plain": "The k-fold Chinese Remainder Theorem in its canonical dependent-product (Pi-type) form, indexed symmetrically by Fin k. For a pairwise-coprime family ns : Fin k → ℕ, the ring ZMod (∏ i, ns i) is isomorphic to the dependent product ∀ i : Fin k, ZMod (ns i). This answers the third open question of the parent k-fold CRT entry, which proved the list/nested-pair form ZMod ns.prod ≃+* CRTProd ns with a right-associated PUnit tower. The Pi-type form is the standard textbook statement and is reusable as an indexed product (no nested pairs). Constructed directly by induction on k: the base case uses that ZMod 1 and the empty Pi-type are both subsingletons; the step splits off the head ns 0 via Fin.prod_univ_succ, applies the binary ZMod.chineseRemainder with head-coprime-to-tail-product, recurses, and reassembles with a Fin.cons ring isomorphism. Includes bijectivity, ring-hom properties, a round-trip identity, the cardinality consequence |∏ᵢ ZMod nᵢ| = ∏ nᵢ, and a concrete ℤ/30ℤ ≅ ∏ ℤ/[2,3,5]ᵢℤ example.",
    "whyMatters": []
  },
  "knownResults": {
    "proven": [
      "crtPi: the k-fold CRT ring isomorphism ZMod (∏ i, ns i) ≃+* ∀ i : Fin k, ZMod (ns i), by induction on k",
      "finSplitRingEquiv: the Fin.cons ring isomorphism (∀ i : Fin (k+1), M i) ≃+* M 0 × (∀ i : Fin k, M i.succ), with map_mul'/map_add' true by rfl",
      "ringEquivOfSubsingleton: any two subsingleton commutative rings are ring-isomorphic — the k = 0 base case",
      "head_coprime_tail_prod: head ns 0 coprime to the tail product ∏ i : Fin k, ns i.succ from pairwise coprimality",
      "crtPi_card: cardinality preservation Nat.card (∀ i, ZMod (ns i)) = ∏ i, ns i for positive moduli",
      "crt235: concrete ℤ/30ℤ ≅ ∏_{i:Fin 3} ZMod ([2,3,5] i)"
